##=========================================================================
##
##
##			Section 1: Model Run Parameters
##
##
##=========================================================================

## Time Variables
## --------------

STARTDATE:                Starting time (MM/DD/YYYY/HH/MM)
06/01/2002/00/00

RUNTIME:                  Simulation length in hours
143183

TIMESTEP:                 Unsaturated zone computational time step (mins)
3.75

GWSTEP:                   Saturated zone computational time step (mins)
30.0

METSTEP:                  Meteorological data time step (mins)
60.0

RAININTRVL:               Time interval in rainfall input (hours)
1

OPINTRVL:                 Output interval (hours)
1

SPOPINTRVL:               Spatial output interval (hours)
8760

INTSTORMMAX:              Interstorm interval (hours)
100

RAINSEARCH:               Rainfall search interval (hours)
24

## Routing Variables
## -----------------

BASEFLOW:                 Baseflow discharge (m3/s)
0.2

KINEMVELCOEF:             Kinematic routing velocity coefficient
3

FLOWEXP:                  Nonlinear discharge coefficient
0.3

CHANNELROUGHNESS:         Uniform channel roughness value
0.03

CHANNELWIDTH:             Uniform channel width  (meters)
12

CHANNELWIDTHCOEFF:        Coefficient in width-area relationship
2.33

CHANNELWIDTHEXPNT:        Exponent in width-area relationship
0.54

CHANNELWIDTHFILE:         Filename that contains channel widths
None


##=========================================================================
##
##
##			Section 2: Model Run Options
##
##
##  OPTMESHINPUT:         1  tMesh data
##                        2  Point Triangulator
##
##  RAINSOURCE:           1  Gridded Rainfall
##                        2  Rain gauges
##
##  OPTEVAPOTRANS:        0  Inactive evapotranspiration
##                        1  Penman-Monteith method
##                        2  Pan evaporation measurements
##
##  OPTSNOW:              0  Inactive snow module
##                        1  Single layer snow module
##
##  HILLALBOPT:           0  Snow albedo for hillslopes
##                        1  Land-cover albedo for hillslopes
##                        2  Dynamic albedo for hillslopes
##
##  OPTRADSHELT:          0  Local controls on shortwave radiation
##                        1  Remote controls on diffuse shortwave
##                        2  Remote controls on entire shortwave
##                        3  No sheltering
##
##  OPTINTERCEPT:         0  Inactive interception
##                        1  Canopy water balance method
##
##  OPTLANDUSE:           0  ID Map with Lookup Table (LANDTABLENAME, LANDMAPNAME)
##                        1  Dynamic updating of gridded parameter maps, ID Map & Table for non-gridded parameters (LUGRID)
##                        2  Static gridded parameter maps, ID Map & Table for non-gridded parameters (LUGRID)
##
##  OPTLUINTERP:          0  Constant (previous) values between land cover
##                        1  Linear interpolation between land cover
##
##  GFLUXOPTION:          0  Inactive ground heat flux
##                        1  Temperature gradient method
##                        2  Force-Restore method
##
##  METDATAOPTION:        0  Inactive meteorological data
##                        1  Weather station point data
##                        2  Gridded meteorological data
##
##  OPTBEDROCK:           0  Uniform bedrock depth (DEPTHTOBEDROCK)
##                        1  Spatial grid of bedrock depth (BEDROCKFILE)
##
##  WIDTHINTERPOLATION:   0  Interpolate between measured and observed
##                        1  Interpolate only between measured
##
##  OPTGWFILE:            0  Resample ASCII grid file in GWATERFILE
##                        1  Read in Voronoi polygon file with GW levels
##
##  OPTGROUNDWATER:       0  Inactive groundwater module
##                        1  Active groundwater module
##
##  OPTSPATIAL:           0  Inactive spatial outputs
##                        1  Active spatial outputs at interval SPOPINTRVL
##
##  OPTRUNON:             0  Inactive runon module
##                        1  Active runon module [IN DEVELOPMENT]
##
##  OPTRESERVOIR:         0  Inactive reservoir routing module
##                        1  Active level pool reservoir routing module
##
##  OPTSOILTYPE:          0  ID Map with Lookup Table (SOILTABLENAME, SOILMAPNAME)
##                        1  Static gridded parameter maps, ID Map & Table for non-gridded parameters (SCGRID)
##
##  OPTPERCOLATION:       0  Inactive channel transmission losses
##                        1  Constant loss method
##                        2  Transient loss method
##                        3  Green-Ampt loss method [IN DEVELOPMENT]
##
##=========================================================================

OPTMESHINPUT:             Mesh input data option
2

RAINSOURCE:               Rainfall data source option
2

OPTEVAPOTRANS:            Option for evapoTranspiration scheme
1

OPTSNOW:                  Option for snow module
1

HILLALBOPT:               Option for albedo of surrounding hillslopes
0

OPTRADSHELT:              Option for local and remote radiation sheltering
0

OPTINTERCEPT:             Option for interception scheme
1

OPTLANDUSE:               Option for static or dynamic land cover
0

OPTLUINTERP:              Option for interpolation of land cover
0

GFLUXOPTION:              Option for ground heat flux
2

METDATAOPTION:            Option for meteorological data
1

OPTBEDROCK:               Option for uniform or variable depth
0

WIDTHINTERPOLATION:       Option for interpolating width values
0

OPTGWFILE:                Option for groundwater initial file
0

OPTGROUNDWATER:           Option for groundwater module
1

OPTSPATIAL:               Option for writing spatial outputs
1

OPTRUNON:                 Option for runon in overland flow paths
0

OPTRESERVOIR:             Option for level pool reservoir routing
0

OPTSOILTYPE:              Option for soil input type
0

OPTPERCOLATION:           Option for percolation losses from channels
0


##=========================================================================
##
##
##			Section 3: Model Input Files and Pathnames
##
##
##=========================================================================

## Mesh Generation
## ---------------

INPUTDATAFILE:            tMesh input file base name for Mesh files, see OPTMESHINPUT
None

POINTFILENAME:            tMesh input file name Points files, see OPTMESHINPUT
data/HappyJack.points

## Resampling Grids
## ----------------

SOILTABLENAME:            Soil parameter reference table (*.sdt), see OPTSOILTYPE
data/HJ_Soil_Table.sdt

SOILMAPNAME:              Soil texture ASCII grid (*.soi), see OPTSOILTYPE
data/HJ_Soil_Map.soi

LANDTABLENAME:            Land use parameter reference table, see OPTLANDUSE
data/HJ_Veg_Table.ldt

LANDMAPNAME:              Land use ASCII grid (*.lan), see OPTLANDUSE
data/HJ_Veg_Map.lan

GWATERFILE:               Ground water ASCII grid (*iwt), see OPTGWFILE
data/HJ_Water_Table_Map.iwt

DEMFILE:                  DEM ASCII grid for sky and land view factors (*.dem), see OPTRADSHELT
data/Sheltering_DEM.dem

RAINFILE:                 Base name of the radar ASCII grid, see RAINSOURCE
None

RAINEXTENSION:            Extension for the radar ASCII grid, see RAINSOURCE
None

RAINDISTRIBUTION:         Precipitation distributed as provided or mean areal precipitation, see RAINSOURCE
0

DEPTHTOBEDROCK:           Uniform depth to bedrock (meters), see OPTBEDROCK
15

BEDROCKFILE:              Bedrock depth ASCII grid (*.brd), see OPTBEDROCK
data/model/depth_to_bedrock.brd

LUGRID:                   Land cover grid data file (*.gdf), see OPTLANDUSE
data/Dynamic_Veg_Grid_Data.gdf

SCGRID:                   Soil cover grid data file (*.gdf), see OPTSOILTYPE
None


## Meteorological Variables
## ------------------------

TLINKE:                   Atmospheric turbidity parameter
2.5

TEMPLAPSE:                Temperature lapse rate
-0.0065

PRECLAPSE:                Precipitation lapse rate
0

UTCOFFSET:                UTC (GMT) offset of the watershed centroid, used for solar position calculations (hours)
-7

CENTROIDLAT:              Latitude of the watershed centroid, used for solar position calculations (decimal degrees)
34.75

CENTROIDLONG:             Longitude of the watershed centroid, used for solar position calculations (decimal degrees)
-111.42

## Meteorological Data
## -------------------

HYDROMETSTATIONS:         Hydrometeorological station file (*.sdf), see METDATAOPTION
data/HJ_WEATHER_2002-2018.sdf

HYDROMETGRID:             Hydrometeorological grid data file (*.gdf), see METDATAOPTION


GAUGESTATIONS:            Rain Gauge station file (*.sdf), see RAINSOURCE
data/HJ_PRECIP_2002-2018.sdf

## Output Data
## -----------

OUTFILENAME:              Filepath and base name of model outputs
results/test/hj_test

NODEOUTPUTLIST:           Filename with Nodes for Dynamic Output (*.nol)
data/Nodes/pNodes.dat

HYDRONODELIST:            Filename with Nodes for HydroModel Output (*.nol)
None

OUTLETNODELIST:           Filename with Interior Nodes for  Output (*.nol)
None

## Module Input Files
## ------------------

RESPOLYGONID:             Path to file of node IDs representing reservoirs, see OPTRESERVOIR


RESDATA:                  Path to file of elevation-discharge-storage information for each type of reservoir, see OPTRESERVOIR


SNOWFILENAME:             Snow parameter reference file (*.spf), see OPTSNOW
data/model/snow_params.spf


##=========================================================================
##
##
##			Section 4: Model Modes
##
##
##=========================================================================

## Channel Transmission Losses
## ---------------------------

CHANNELCONDUCTIVITY:      Conductivity in channel for all methods (mm/hr)
0

TRANSIENTCONDUCTIVITY:    Conductivity in channel during transient period in (mm/hr)
0

TRANSIENTTIME:            Time until transient period ends (hours)
0

CHANNELPOROSITY:          Porosity in channel
0

CHANPOREINDEX:            Channel pore index in channel
0

CHANPSIB:                 Matric potential in channel
0


##=========================================================================
##
##
##			Section 5: Restart Mode Options
##
##
##  RESTARTMODE:   0  No reading or writing of restart
##                 1  Write files (only for initial runs)
##                 2  Read file only (to start at some specified time)
##                 3  Read a restart file and continue to write
##
##=========================================================================

RESTARTMODE:              Restart Mode Option
0

RESTARTINTRVL:            Time set for restart output (hours)
None

RESTARTDIR:               Path of directory for restart output
None

RESTARTFILE:              Actual file to restart a run
None

##=========================================================================
##
##
##			Section 6: Parallel Mode Options
##
##
##  PARALLELMODE:   0  Run in serial mode
##                  1  Run in parallel mode
##                  2  Generate partition only with summary statistics
##
##  GRAPHOPTION:    Reach-graph partitioning method (used to generate the
##                  partition when no GRAPHFILE exists yet):
##                  0  SurfaceFlow (SF): flow edges only
##                  1  Surface-Subsurface Flow (SSF): flow + subsurface flux
##                  2  Surface-Subsurface Flow w/ Headwaters (SSF-H):
##                     SSF plus balancing of headwater reaches
##
##  GRAPHFILE:      Path to the reach graph file. If the file exists it is
##                  read; if it does not, tRIBS generates the partition
##                  in-process with METIS (using GRAPHOPTION above) and
##                  writes for reuse. The partition is always sized
##                  to the number of MPI processes.
##
##=========================================================================

PARALLELMODE:             Serial Mode, Parallel, or Partitioning Mode Option
0

GRAPHOPTION:              Reach partitioning method
0

GRAPHFILE:                Reach connectivity filename
None

